A quoted :INHERIT parent. The statement takes a name, and a class with
the parent written as a string does not compile (verified on STARLIMS 12,
issue #372), so diag.inherit_qualified_name reports the string and gives
the statement to write. The formatter leaves the string as written.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Counter;
:INHERIT "Samples.BaseCounter";
:DECLARE nCount;

:PROCEDURE Reset;
	Me:nCount := 0;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS Counter;
:INHERIT "Samples.BaseCounter";
:DECLARE nCount;

:PROCEDURE Reset;
	Me:nCount := 0;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
2:10-2:31 error inherit_qualified_name: ':INHERIT' takes the parent as a name, not a string, and a quoted parent does not compile: write ':INHERIT Samples.BaseCounter;'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:10-2:31 error inherit_qualified_name: ':INHERIT' takes the parent as a name, not a string, and a quoted parent does not compile: write ':INHERIT Samples.BaseCounter;'
